    "note": "A long double-deck bridge crosses the Brahmaputra on paired concrete shafts and wide pier bases. Repeated steel trusses enclose both lower tracks. A dark three-lane highway with striped barriers and single-arm lamps runs above them. The 99 m sea-level datum uses the standard viewer terrain and PMTiles water. The upper road joins the clipped NH15 approaches. Independent lower rail embankments follow the two mapped track alignments, and the two lower service crossings remain open. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
